course: dictionary
lesson: 14992
title: Reproduction: three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around them tells you which one you need. Reproduction is a good example. Look at the clues in the sentence first: are we talking about living things, a copy, or sound and pictures?
explain: «Reproduction is how living things make new young of their own kind.» Here the clues are living things and young, so reproduction is a life process, like breathing and growing.
explain: «The shop sold a reproduction of an old clock.» The clue is a copy of something old, so a reproduction is a copy and not the real thing. Try it: swap in "copy" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «The speakers gave a clear reproduction of the singer's voice.» Sound is the clue here, so reproduction means a copy of a sound, like a recording.
fact: Reproduction means the way living things make new living things of their own kind.
fact: Plants reproduce by seeds, runners and bulbs. Animals reproduce by laying eggs or having live young.
fact: «A reproduction» is a copy of something, such as a painting, not the original.
fact: Reproduction can also mean making a copy of sound or pictures, like «a reproduction of the song».
fact: Reproduction as a life process is not countable, but a reproduction as a copy can be counted: «a reproduction, two reproductions».
exercise: «Plants can reproduce by seeds, runners and bulbs.» What does reproduce mean here? | Grow very tall in the sun | *Make new plants of their own kind | Lose their leaves in winter | Change colour in autumn
exercise: «The shop sold a reproduction of an old clock.» What is a reproduction here? | The oldest clock in the world | A clock that has stopped working | *A copy of the old clock | A clock made of gold
exercise: «The speakers gave a clear reproduction of the drums.» What does reproduction mean here? | *A copy of the sound | A new drum kit for the band | A loud noise from the street | A game played with drums
test:
Which of these is an example of reproduction in animals? | *A hen laying eggs | A tree losing its leaves | A puppy growing its first teeth | A fish changing colour
«The museum had a reproduction of a famous painting, but the real painting was in another room.» What does reproduction mean here? | Only the real painting | *A copy of the painting | A painting that has been cleaned | A painting in a frame
exam: Which meaning of reproduction is used in «Ferns reproduce by spores»? | A recording of wind in the trees | Growing a fern in a pot | A copy of a fern in a picture | *Making new ferns of their own kind
